Z||000007||HugGRRRFiero||08-08-2000||07:41 AM||||  A 2 seater eh' WOW  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">, No kidding, I've been looking all over for one of those...<P>  Well, I believe SE is for Special Edition, so yours has got to be very special!<P>  Take a second and post the VIN number, these guys can tell you exactly what you've got.<P>Brent<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||12
Z||000008||Patrick's Dad||08-08-2000||08:20 AM||||In the words of the guy who signs my paycheck, "Most (of these people) deserve your sense of humor, but let them get to know you, first."<P>Yes, I'm the guy who, when asked, "Can I ask you a question?" says, "You just did." (and I'm in retail).<P>The core of this message is, maybe Fiero86 is a newbie, and, in deference to the fact that we're all Fiero lovers here, albeit of differing levels, let's give him a chance. In other words, "Can't we all just get along?"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So, as to F86; If your sail panel (The trangular, black plastic panel right behind the window) says "SE," then you've got an SE, an upscale trim level of the Fiero. If, on the rear end of the decklid (Engine cover), it reads "Fiero GT," then you've got a GT, (Which in 1986, as it has been established on this forum, can be fastback or notchback) the HiPo model. If it reads "Fiero 2M4," then you've got a garden variety Fiero, though none of us would think of our babies this way.<P>In fairness to the yuksters here on the forum, you didn't lead with much information. I have another car in my driveway that has a V8 and a trunk, can you tell me what it is? Take the humor for what it is, and consider yourself initiated. Take a read around, and most of your questions will be answered. If you still have them, by all means ask, but be prepared for the love of you fellow Fiero-ites.<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Xtreme Fiero's||08-08-2000||08:53 AM||||Um...... What if your car says SE on the 1/4 window and Fiero 2m4 on the deck lid  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Gold-86SE||08-08-2000||09:18 AM||||<BR>I am considering that Xtreme's question is a serious one, SE on the sail and 2m4 on the tail, means you have a 1984 SE, top-of-the-line for that year, except for the limited production replica of the Indy Pace Car.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000011||HugGRRRFiero||08-08-2000||10:59 AM||||Fiero86,<P>   I just seen that you had another thread going on the same subject "what kind of car do I have?"  I'm very Sorry about the sarcasm, I was just replying only to limited information you gave here.  I didn't know that your Fiero was a kit and you trying to find out what kind of Fiero was originally under it.<P>  Welcome...  I'm fairly new to the forum too, if you're going to post a reply, just post it in the topic you created, don't post a new topic with the same subject or you'll just have us scratching our heads trying to figure out what's going on.<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||10
