Z||000025||dman||08-10-2000||03:16 AM||||Hello Fiero86. I've never heard of a Piranha kit. Over the years there have been many kit cars based on the Fiero. Many kits are replicas of existing cars. The most common fiero based kits would be the Ferrari replicas: 308, 328, 355, Testarossa, 512TR.<P>I have a 328 and I'm currently building a Testarossa (but I'm thinking of updating it to be like the newer 512TR, I'm also contemplating making it a convertible).<P>Lamborghini replicas are also common (Countach and Diablo).<P>Those are the most common (or should I say the ones most often copied). There have been a few more though that are of original design or 'inspired' by some other type of sports car. The Aldino, DL10 Predator, Artero, etc.<P>Back to your question, do you have a decent kit? I think the answer is entirely subjective. Do you like it? Then yes, you have a decent kit.<P>If you want more info about kit cars you can go to the following web sites:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.kitkar.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitkar.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.kitcars.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitcars.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.kitcar.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitcar.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.kitcarlinks.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitcarlinks.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.kitcarlinks.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitcarlinks.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com/fierohq.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com/fierohq.html</A> <P>Oh one last thing, in another thread here on the forum someone posted a picture of the very nice looking custom interior. Someone described that interior as being from a Russian made kit named the Pyrahna. Could that possibly be your car? Go here and take a look:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003193.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003193.html</A> <P><BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||Patrick's Dad||08-10-2000||02:31 PM||||Monk and Stimp, I don't necessarily want to go looking thru the archives, either. Heck, I couldn't even get in last night.... I thought I remember a member, Fiero86GT or with simialr nomenclature, commenting that he knew that the '86 GT came in a notchback, because he had one. Not that I've ever been wrong before....  ;-)<P>As to the Phyrana, I think it's a neat kit, even the wing (Commented on above mentioned thread.). I'm not hot on kits right now, as I think that the Fiero is unique enough not to mess with it, but I won't knock on anyone who makes their car just that bit more.<P>Peace!<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
